    {
      "title": "California and New York sue over Trump push to halt wind energy projects",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/california-new-york-trump-wind-energy",
      "description": "<p>US officials have begun to buy back wind leases as president seek to block renewables in favor of fossil fuels</p><p>Democratic attorneys general from California and New York have sued the Trump administration over its plans to buy back offshore wind leases as Donald Trump seeks to discourage the expansion of wind energy in favor of fossil fuels.</p><p>California attorney general Rob Bonta said he was suing over removal of a project off his state’s coast planned by Chicago-based Invenergy. The Trump administration said in June it was buying back the company’s US offshore wind leases for four wind projects on the east and west coasts.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2026/sep/22/california-new-york-trump-wind-energy\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-22T21:35:42"
    },
    {
      "title": "India on track to add about 8 GW wind energy capacity in FY27: MNRE",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/india-news/india-on-track-to-add-about-8-gw-wind-energy-capacity-in-fy27-mnre-126092201130_1.html",
      "description": "India is on track to achieve 7.5-8 GW wind energy capacity addition in the current fiscal year, a senior official said on Tuesday.\nAddressing the EU-India Wind Energy Business Summit 2026 at WindEnergy Hamburg, Rajesh Kulhari, Joint Secretary in the Ministry of New & Renewable Energy, said that India has added over 6 GW of wind energy capacity in 2025-26.\nHe exuded confidence that India is on track to achieve 7.5 to 8 GW of wind energy capacity in 2026-27.\nIndia aims to have over 100 GW of wind energy capacity by 2030. It has installed wind generation capacity of 58.52 GW as of August 31, 2026.\nIndia has added 2.42 GW of wind energy capacity till August 31 in the current fiscal year (April to August).\nThe wind energy capacity addition is important as India has set an ambitious target of achieving 500 GW of renewable energy.\nKulhari also assured full cooperation to the EU in the renewable energy sector.",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-09-22T14:47:20"
    }
  ]
